{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>By day</b> — He likened the city to a circle. He said that חמס (violence) and עי׳ surrounds it — this is the surrounding line, and און (iniquity) and עמל (trouble) is the point, and this is the meaning of בקרבה (in her midst)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 55, :notes {0 "The lemma is יומם but the comment discusses phrase structure from the verse; עי׳ appears to be a truncated word, likely עיון or similar; translated hyper-literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:13.345362968Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}